    {
      "id": "models",
      "title": "DeciLM dispatch and heterogeneous block construction",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "The earlier architecture entry describes dispatch and checkpoint mapping through shared modules. This change extends that design with a dedicated DeciLM configuration and model pair.",
          "basis": "ancestor",
          "evidence": ["call_24f6ff4abcf74f659798c84ef820c66d"]
        },
        {
          "text": "DeciLMConfig requires block_configs to contain exactly num_hidden_layers entries. It retains global hidden width and query-head count, derives head_dim by integer division when absent or false, accepts SiLU or an omitted hidden_act, and requests the shared NEOX-style RoPE settings.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_3d078f61ff7049a9830e644a7d7ae503", "call_73a16df97e744641a62ffa999c39b395"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Each block reads attention and ffn dictionaries. A truthy no_op omits that branch and its norm; otherwise attention receives n_heads_in_group as num_kv_heads, while the MLP receives a block-specific intermediate width. Shared TransformerBlock.forward conditionally executes present branches with residual additions.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_3d078f61ff7049a9830e644a7d7ae503", "call_a31570fc45044da798110cf27eedecc8"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Active attention branches reject sink-token, linear-replacement, sparsification, unshifted-sink and prefill-window-in-sink options through assertions; active FFNs reject linear replacement and sparsification. These checks occur after the no_op decision, so omitted branches bypass them.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_3d078f61ff7049a9830e644a7d7ae503"]
        },
        {
